# THE PINNED COLLECTOR DISTRIBUTIONS, decided once.
#
# ADR 0014 made this a decision rather than a version to bump: the Gateway runs the
# contrib distribution because Spill needs `file_storage` and the Pipeline Guardrail
# needs `transform`, and an Agent runs core because it needs neither and a smaller
# attack surface next to every service is worth having.
#
# Two consumers read this file, and that is the reason it exists:
#
#   harness/docker-compose.yaml            stands the topology up and moves OTLP
#                                          through it.
#   .github/scripts/validate-compiled-configs.sh
#                                          the Distribution Check — every compiled
#                                          configuration loaded and started by the
#                                          distribution it is compiled for, on every
#                                          pull request.
#
# Pinned in one place because the two must agree. A harness proving a config runs on
# 0.127.0 while CI checked it against something else would be two answers to one
# question, and the wrong one would be the one nobody ran.
#
# Both images carry the SAME version, deliberately: the split under test is core
# versus contrib, and a version difference would confound it.
COLLECTOR_CORE_IMAGE=otel/opentelemetry-collector:0.127.0
COLLECTOR_CONTRIB_IMAGE=otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.127.0
